                <pb facs="0782" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1477a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Harbin</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-20T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Report by telegram in what respects and to what degree Russian functions in
                    regard to (1) actual control of the Chinese Eastern Railway and (2) municipal
                    administration in railway zone have been taken over by Chinese or other
                    non-Russian agencies.</p>
                <p>Department desires not only a general view of the situation but also specific
                    instances in brief for its information. Make reply complete but avoid
                    unnecessary length.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
